From 6215858c3817b6d3699bbd4fe794415c0b2b6177 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 02:42:56 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Make lifecycle execution proofs portable across Bash
 versions

Separate oversized script fixture creation from the Bash-version-dependent
execution proof. Select Bash from PATH consistently in the heredoc harness
and corpus; supply a harness-local timeout fallback and key execution-only
premises to verified grammar/tool/platform capabilities. All scanner refusal
assertions and generated-corpus security properties remain unconditional.
No production or platforms-marker changes.

Root (happened): the subscript scanner fixture existed only when its optional
execution proof ran; heredoc proof premises assumed Bash 5 and GNU tools even
though the harness hardcoded /bin/bash and restricted PATH.
Root (not caught): these files lack platforms markers, so the macOS CI lane
excluded them. Coverage ownership remains t_5e88b2513095504c.
Recurrence: follows the existing name-indirection version-keyed proof pattern;
reproduced the reported failures independently on current main 6b554713f2.

Proof (native macOS, canonical hermes-core-wt test --local):
- Unpatched 6b554713f2: heredoc 241 passed/12 failed with both PATH selections;
  subscript Bash 3.2 97 passed/1 failed; Bash 5.3.9 98 passed.
- Patched Bash 3.2.57: heredoc 253 passed; subscript 98 passed.
- Patched Bash 5.3.9: heredoc 253 passed; subscript 98 passed.
- Mutant reverting fixture ordering: exact printf -v heredoc case fails again
  on Bash 3.2 (97 passed/1 failed); patch restored after the check.
- Independent source review found no weakened security assertion.
Linux-native shared-helper consumer checks and required CI run on pool landing
owner before publication/merge. This Mac supplies native proof and git bundle.
